From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0143-lower-the-remaining-ocarina-compute-forms.patch

Source: 0143-lower-the-remaining-ocarina-compute-forms.patch
shader: lower the remaining Ocarina compute forms


- ULDC with an index register: U8 and U16, signed offsets and any immediate, since the
  register can align it. Comes with Lichii's direct U8/U16 ULDC form, which ours did not
  have either (Star Fox there); the direct form keeps its range and alignment checks.
- ULEA: the carry out can be any UPn. Our UIADD3 already takes any UPn.
- F2IP.U8.F32: a second byte source and the default rounding.
- I2F.U8 from a uniform register: any byte selector.

Left out: the P2R change. It teaches Lichii's write_count, which this tree has no copy
of; our call link proof marks bits 16-23 of every prior instruction as written, so P2R
already counts as one write. UIADD3's carry hunk is here already. The test files of the
PR do not exist in this tree.

Added here: F2IP's Ra (bit 24) in PrepareRegisterPressure, which was only reachable as
RZ before. Lichii's table still lacks it, so a reserved Ra would read the mirror there.

The PR marks two things as inferred, not checked on hardware: F2IP's byte order and
rounding, and that an unaligned indexed ULDC reads the aligned word. Lichii also notes
that without its vegetation commits these programs may never be reached. None of our
saved run logs shows a rejection by these forms: Ocarina's rejected programs all stop
at op 23c (matrix multiply) first, so they could still come after it.

